            <ArticleTitle>Enterovirus 68 Infection--Association with Asthma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>226-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jaip.2015.12.013</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S2213-2198(16)00002-7</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A previously sporadic virus called enterovirus 68 (EV-D68) appears to have been associated with asthma-like illness with a predisposition for asthmatics after an outbreak that occurred in North America in 2014. Clinicians should be aware of the clinical associations with EV-D68 particularly its predilection with pre-existing asthma or asthma-like illness as well as the potential association with acute flaccid myelitis. Further elucidation and development of diagnostic and treatments modalities are warranted to better understand and limit the potential public health impact of future outbreaks of EV-D68 infection.</AbstractText>
